    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d392">

                <pb facs="0326" n="252" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg252"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 99.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 4, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your despatch No. 60, of
                    the 17th instant, relative to the refusal of the French government to permit Mr.
                    Hammond, agent of the American Emigration Company at Havre, to contract for the
                    transport of emigrants through Havre to the United States. You may ask for
                    explanations from Mr. Drouyn de Lhuys, but you will not make it a subject of
                    protest or remonstrance without instructions.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
